WEBVTT

00:18.268 --> 00:20.186
Taiyo, save me!

00:20.812 --> 00:24.566
Can't even protect one woman.

00:25.358 --> 00:26.693
So pathetic.

00:27.694 --> 00:30.071
Mutsumi...

00:35.035 --> 00:36.036
Mutsumi!

00:38.705 --> 00:40.040
A dream?

00:41.166 --> 00:44.169
Right. I...

00:54.429 --> 00:56.014
Hey, sorry!

00:56.097 --> 01:01.394
Owwww!

01:03.855 --> 01:05.398
Oh, dear.

01:13.698 --> 01:20.413
YOZAKURA FAMILY

02:39.701 --> 02:40.702
PLAN 3
FEELINGS

02:40.785 --> 02:41.870
Okay! You're all set!

02:41.953 --> 02:44.164
Sorry to bug you this early. Thanks!

02:44.664 --> 02:47.041
I'm the one who should be apologizing.

02:47.500 --> 02:51.462
I'd asked Goliath to stand guard over you

02:51.546 --> 02:54.674
so that Big Bro Kyoichiro wouldn't
assault you in your sleep again, but...

03:01.306 --> 03:04.184
<i>She's right.
I wouldn't put it past him.</i>

03:07.562 --> 03:09.564
You know you're not supposed to hurt him!

03:12.108 --> 03:14.110
M-Mutsumi! Don't do that, or--

03:15.862 --> 03:20.158
It's all right. Goliath would never
attack the head of the family.

03:21.409 --> 03:23.453
Whoa!

03:33.713 --> 03:37.800
So? What's this favor
that you want to ask of me?

03:39.177 --> 03:41.930
I want you to make me stronger.

03:43.890 --> 03:46.517
<i>Right, so that's
what this is about, huh?</i>

03:47.435 --> 03:48.811
No worries.

03:48.895 --> 03:52.899
We're planning to train you bit by bit,
to accommodate your ordinariness.

03:52.982 --> 03:55.443
That would take too long!
Hmm?

03:55.735 --> 04:00.114
The other day, it was all I could do
to get Mutsumi out of danger's way.

04:00.823 --> 04:03.660
One false move,
and I might have ended up dead myself.

04:04.452 --> 04:06.788
Even though Mutsumi chose me...

04:09.582 --> 04:12.126
...thank you for marrying me!

04:12.210 --> 04:13.503
<i>And also...</i>

04:15.588 --> 04:17.757
I want to become strong for Mutsumi!

04:19.968 --> 04:20.969
So...

04:21.177 --> 04:22.178
Whoa!

04:22.512 --> 04:24.264
I wouldn't overstep if I were you.

04:24.347 --> 04:25.556
Whoa!

04:25.640 --> 04:28.685
I know my physique's
nothing to write home about,

04:28.768 --> 04:31.145
but I have a talent
for aikido and jujitsu.

04:31.729 --> 04:35.066
I started training at three
and went on my first mission at six.

04:35.566 --> 04:39.237
In other words, even armed with
Yozakura talent, it takes three years.

04:39.737 --> 04:42.991
An ordinary human
would require even more time.

04:46.202 --> 04:49.789
If you think that you can get by
on emotion, you're just being naive.

04:52.834 --> 04:56.337
That said, the way you feel
so strongly about Mutsumi...

04:57.255 --> 04:58.756
I don't want that to go to waste.

04:59.340 --> 05:03.428
The Yozakura-style all-out training...
Want to give it a try?

05:04.262 --> 05:05.388
Are you serious?

05:06.139 --> 05:08.850
But there is just one condition.

05:09.434 --> 05:11.686
I want you to live in this mansion
for one month.

05:12.145 --> 05:13.980
Huh? Is that all?

05:14.397 --> 05:18.151
Thanks to our disorderly conduct,
your home got wrecked, after all.

05:18.860 --> 05:22.280
Think of it as a rehearsal,
and just live here. That's all.

05:23.406 --> 05:25.575
Your training will begin
one month from now!

05:26.034 --> 05:27.285
Thank you very much!

05:36.836 --> 05:38.755
Oh. Sorry about that.

05:38.838 --> 05:40.715
Forgot to mention one thing.

05:41.716 --> 05:46.804
<i>This mansion is rigged all over the place
with traps for spy training.</i>

05:48.097 --> 05:52.393
Meaning that in the Yozakura house,
daily life itself is training.

05:53.936 --> 05:56.147
If you don't master
this beginner-level stuff fast,

05:56.230 --> 05:59.025
all-out training
will only be a pipe dream for you.

06:00.943 --> 06:04.197
First off,
give it all you've got for one month.

06:05.114 --> 06:07.992
<i>I might end up dead in one day.</i>

06:17.377 --> 06:19.754
Ugh, be quiet.

06:32.308 --> 06:34.811
Whoa!

06:35.395 --> 06:37.105
Whoa!

06:41.651 --> 06:43.194
Are you all right?

06:43.277 --> 06:45.363
That woke you up right away, didn't it?

06:45.446 --> 06:48.449
It's to help you get up
in a flash at any time.

06:48.533 --> 06:51.369
I knew it was asking too much
to have you live here.

06:51.452 --> 06:52.870
I'm so worried.

06:54.372 --> 06:56.541
Should we get ready for the funeral?

06:59.502 --> 07:01.087
I was only kidding.

07:02.713 --> 07:05.133
I don't know how you manage
to live here, Mutsumi.

07:05.216 --> 07:08.469
The traps in this house
don't activate for me.

07:08.553 --> 07:09.554
Huh?

07:09.637 --> 07:14.392
If you're accepted by the house, you can
set them not to go off on you, either.

07:14.475 --> 07:17.145
"Accepted by the house"?

07:17.228 --> 07:18.229
Right.

07:18.855 --> 07:23.401
<i>All of the traps in this house
are controlled by a computer.</i>

07:24.026 --> 07:28.573
<i>So if you clear them all and get accepted
as a member of the Yozakura family,</i>

07:28.656 --> 07:31.617
<i>you can then turn them on or off at will.</i>

07:34.370 --> 07:35.913
In layman's terms,

07:35.997 --> 07:39.417
it's like getting a god-mode bonus
when you clear all the levels.

07:40.042 --> 07:43.629
When we're injured or it's a hassle,
we keep them off, too.

07:44.130 --> 07:47.717
Even a normal person could clear them
in two years or so, so have at it!

07:47.800 --> 07:49.093
T-Two years?

07:51.471 --> 07:52.597
M-My stomach...

07:52.680 --> 07:56.225
Always be on the alert.
Meals are also part of your training.

07:57.810 --> 08:01.981
To build up tolerance, everyone's
food except for Big Sis Mutsumi's

08:02.064 --> 08:04.233
is laced with a little poison.

08:04.650 --> 08:08.362
But don't worry!
It's only enough to give you the runs.

08:08.446 --> 08:10.740
<i>What the heck is that?</i>

08:12.658 --> 08:15.328
Are you kidding me?

08:23.794 --> 08:26.297
<i>I should've known. Damn it!</i>

08:26.923 --> 08:29.800
In order to get inside the bathroom,
you'll need to pick the lock

08:29.884 --> 08:33.763
and crack the password
that refreshes every minute.

08:34.305 --> 08:35.640
Mutsumi, hold up.

08:35.723 --> 08:36.724
But...

08:37.099 --> 08:41.062
Hey, how about that
early-morning entertainment? I love it!

08:41.145 --> 08:42.146
Oh!

08:42.230 --> 08:43.689
Morning, Mutsumi!

08:43.773 --> 08:46.234
You're the prettiest thing
in the universe again today!

08:46.692 --> 08:48.402
Help me!

08:48.486 --> 08:50.613
Shion, go show him how it's done.

08:50.696 --> 08:51.697
Okay.

08:54.116 --> 08:58.496
<i>And so,
my hellish daily life began.</i>

09:34.740 --> 09:35.741
Mmm!

09:37.535 --> 09:38.536
Oh!

09:42.206 --> 09:44.584
AGILITY

09:55.219 --> 09:57.138
MARKSMANSHIP

10:01.892 --> 10:02.977
POISON TOLERANCE

10:05.229 --> 10:07.023
ANALYTICAL ABILITY

10:15.698 --> 10:17.867
ACCURACY

10:21.245 --> 10:23.789
Asano, are you convulsing?

10:23.873 --> 10:24.874
You okay?

10:24.957 --> 10:26.334
Want some water?

10:26.417 --> 10:27.960
I-I'm okay.

10:33.633 --> 10:34.925
<i>Can't tell them...</i>

10:35.009 --> 10:39.263
<i>that the shirt the Yozakuras gave me
is crazy heavy.</i>

10:39.847 --> 10:43.225
<i>Not like they'd believe me
if I did tell them.</i>

10:44.685 --> 10:46.479
<i>I'm about to sink into my desk...</i>

10:46.562 --> 10:47.730
BASIC PHYSICAL STRENGTH

10:55.071 --> 10:56.280
<i>I'm exhausted.</i>

11:06.832 --> 11:07.833
<i>Mutsumi...</i>

11:08.334 --> 11:09.960
<i>working so late?</i>

11:19.720 --> 11:21.263
Not even close.

11:24.016 --> 11:27.478
Who knew it would be this hard
just to turn on the TV?

11:29.271 --> 11:31.023
All right! One more time.

11:33.109 --> 11:34.110
Taiyo?

11:35.111 --> 11:36.112
Mutsumi.

11:36.612 --> 11:38.656
Why don't you take a little break?

11:40.282 --> 11:42.118
Here. That'll warm you up.

11:42.618 --> 11:43.911
Thanks.

11:43.994 --> 11:47.540
Hey, sorry.
Did I wake you up, by any chance?

11:47.623 --> 11:48.791
No, no.

11:51.127 --> 11:53.421
Taiyo, you're not pushing yourself
too hard, are you?

11:54.755 --> 11:56.590
Huh? Wh-What do you mean?

11:56.674 --> 11:58.676
You don't have to hide it! I can tell!

11:58.759 --> 12:02.722
I'm probably the reason, aren't I?

12:03.013 --> 12:04.890
Hey, no, that's not true.

12:04.974 --> 12:05.975
It's just that I...

12:06.600 --> 12:08.686
You're not weak at all, Taiyo.

12:09.895 --> 12:13.482
After all, Taiyo,
ever since back then, you've been...

12:16.152 --> 12:17.236
Mo--

12:17.319 --> 12:18.362
Oh!

12:18.863 --> 12:20.573
Morning, Taiyo-kun!

12:21.532 --> 12:23.534
Morning, Mutsumi-chan.

12:24.160 --> 12:27.496
<i>We were no more than neighbors then,</i>

12:27.955 --> 12:31.000
<i>and compared to now,
we weren't especially close.</i>

12:31.542 --> 12:34.420
MATRICULATION CEREMONY

12:34.879 --> 12:37.381
<i>The turning point came
when we started junior high.</i>

12:38.174 --> 12:42.470
<i>This curse-like white hair that refused
to submit to any degree of coloring</i>

12:42.970 --> 12:46.474
<i>drew all kinds of looks,
even during our matriculation ceremony.</i>

12:49.685 --> 12:51.645
Yozakura, was it?

12:52.104 --> 12:54.815
What's with that silver streak?
Do you want to stand out?

12:55.316 --> 12:56.734
The color faded, so--

12:56.817 --> 12:58.903
Then just color it, you idiot.

12:59.320 --> 13:01.530
It won't take color, no matter what I do.

13:01.614 --> 13:03.949
Oh? Well, in that case...

13:06.076 --> 13:07.453
why don't you cut it off?

13:07.536 --> 13:09.622
Scary!

13:11.582 --> 13:13.292
H-Hey, what do you think you're doing?

13:17.713 --> 13:19.298
Taiyo-kun! Stop it!

13:19.673 --> 13:21.300
Taiyo-kun! Taiyo-kun!

13:21.675 --> 13:23.093
Taiyo-kun! Do you hear me?

13:26.639 --> 13:27.640
Taiyo!

13:29.767 --> 13:31.227
What's his problem? He's crazy!

13:31.310 --> 13:33.020
Let's get out of here!

13:39.193 --> 13:43.197
The guidance counselor told me
it was too long, so that was good timing.

13:43.697 --> 13:44.907
Taiyo-kun...

13:45.825 --> 13:47.368
You can call me Taiyo.

13:47.451 --> 13:49.745
I mean, you did just now, didn't you?

13:50.329 --> 13:51.831
Sorry. It slipped out.

13:53.249 --> 13:56.001
If anyone tries to do something
to you again, tell me, okay...

13:56.085 --> 13:57.086
Mutsumi.

13:58.546 --> 13:59.547
Okay.

14:02.007 --> 14:06.637
You've been protecting me
all this time. So...

14:10.808 --> 14:13.227
try not to push yourself so hard!

14:37.877 --> 14:38.919
Morning!

14:50.723 --> 14:53.309
So now you can
hit the power button, huh?

14:53.392 --> 14:57.521
But I'm still finding it hard
to change the channel.

14:58.188 --> 15:01.025
You're not holding the grip right.

15:01.108 --> 15:03.527
You should grip it higher.

15:03.611 --> 15:05.487
Then the gun won't recoil as much.

15:05.571 --> 15:06.864
Mmm...

15:07.907 --> 15:08.991
What's wrong?

15:09.074 --> 15:11.619
Hey, so now you can
get the TV to turn on.

15:11.702 --> 15:13.913
Oh.
Big Sis Shion!

15:13.996 --> 15:18.125
Shinzo, here's Taiyo's performance data
that you asked me to analyze.

15:20.920 --> 15:21.962
Thanks.

15:23.756 --> 15:25.966
Both of you, thank you so much.

15:27.092 --> 15:31.347
Um, Big Sis Shion, I've been
wondering about this for a while.

15:31.847 --> 15:34.892
Why does Big Bro Shinzo, uh...

15:34.975 --> 15:38.896
Oh. This one's super-lazy and super-shy,

15:39.563 --> 15:42.816
So he spends most of his time
holed up in that garbage-can tank.

15:42.900 --> 15:44.860
What? Big Bro Shinzo, too?

15:44.944 --> 15:48.614
Says the girl who's always
holed up in her own room.

15:48.697 --> 15:53.661
All right, Taiyo. Weren't you going to
ask Nanao how to deal with poisonous gas?

15:53.744 --> 15:55.245
Hey!

15:55.329 --> 15:57.581
Uh, right. I'll be going now!

16:02.211 --> 16:04.296
He's got talent, you know.

16:04.380 --> 16:07.549
Well, yeah, he sure
isn't advancing at normal speed.

16:09.009 --> 16:10.761
Is it talent...

16:16.350 --> 16:17.476
<i>or something else...</i>

16:21.021 --> 16:23.983
Big Sis, this is way too heavy.

16:24.066 --> 16:26.777
You ditched your dishwashing duties
this morning again, right?

16:26.860 --> 16:28.487
This is to make up for that.

16:28.988 --> 16:30.906
I hate who I was this morning.

16:34.535 --> 16:37.538
One, two... One, two...

16:38.414 --> 16:41.125
The nerve gas
in this AC flows upward,

16:41.208 --> 16:43.127
so if you crawl away, you'll be just fine.

16:43.210 --> 16:44.503
Right!

16:47.297 --> 16:49.133
Hey, look who I found!

16:49.216 --> 16:50.467
Hey, Taiyo--

16:52.136 --> 16:53.971
Come on, keep walking, and look sharp!

16:58.017 --> 16:59.143
<i>And then...</i>

17:02.521 --> 17:03.689
Morning!

17:03.772 --> 17:05.065
Morning, Taiyo!

17:07.901 --> 17:08.902
I'm so impressed!

17:08.986 --> 17:11.780
You can just sail down the stairs
and the hallways now, can't you?

17:11.864 --> 17:14.199
Well, I've been here
for three whole weeks.

17:14.283 --> 17:17.119
Hey, Mutsumi, could you pass me the milk?

17:17.202 --> 17:18.203
Sure!

17:18.287 --> 17:19.288
Thanks.

17:24.251 --> 17:27.588
Gah! It won't open!

17:28.172 --> 17:31.800
Even after staying here for three weeks,
he's hopeless against that door.

17:31.884 --> 17:35.012
Okey-doke, here I come!

17:35.095 --> 17:37.723
I gave him that milk!

17:38.474 --> 17:41.560
It's not your fault, Big Sis.
- Taiyo!

17:41.643 --> 17:43.979
Hey, look, Mutsumi! It's a rattle!

17:44.063 --> 17:47.274
That's not gonna work, Shinzo.
Rattle, rattle!

17:47.357 --> 17:48.358
Taiyo?
- Huh?

17:50.611 --> 17:52.988
Hey, what's wrong? Get ahold of yourself!

17:53.072 --> 17:55.115
Nanao, get him some medicine right away.

17:55.199 --> 17:56.492
O-Okay!

18:03.874 --> 18:05.793
NANAO

18:08.837 --> 18:11.256
It's a fever
brought on by fatigue,

18:11.340 --> 18:13.592
so you'll recover right away
if you stay in bed.

18:14.093 --> 18:15.719
You heard him.

18:15.803 --> 18:19.681
I've already told Mutsumi,
so make sure you rest up.

18:20.182 --> 18:22.101
I-I'm all right.

18:22.851 --> 18:25.145
I'm going to keep living here...

18:25.229 --> 18:26.730
for the one remaining week.

18:29.399 --> 18:30.943
In the shape that you're in?

18:35.114 --> 18:40.077
If you keep carrying on like this,
there's no way you'll ever survive.

18:41.286 --> 18:43.372
You were onto me, then?

18:44.081 --> 18:45.582
Right from the start.

18:46.208 --> 18:48.502
There's no achieving extraordinary results

18:48.585 --> 18:51.130
without resorting
to extraordinary measures.

18:51.964 --> 18:55.259
<i>My guess is...
Shion's data collection and analysis,</i>

18:56.009 --> 18:57.970
<i>Shinzo's training,</i>

18:58.262 --> 19:00.347
<i>Nanao's medical skills
for treating your injuries,</i>

19:00.430 --> 19:03.100
<i>and giving you drugs so that
you could go without sleep or rest,</i>

19:03.183 --> 19:07.646
<i>and Kengo's fake skin technology
to hide your wounds.</i>

19:08.480 --> 19:11.692
Nanao, to think that you of all people

19:11.775 --> 19:15.112
would take part in a suicide mission
like this. You disappoint me.

19:15.195 --> 19:18.115
I'm sorry, Big Sis Futaba.

19:18.782 --> 19:21.368
It's not their fault.

19:21.785 --> 19:22.828
Hmm?

19:23.579 --> 19:26.915
They all tried to stop me,

19:26.999 --> 19:29.835
but I was adamant and pleaded with them.

19:31.044 --> 19:36.300
I told them that I wanted to be able to
protect Mutsumi as soon as possible.

19:40.470 --> 19:41.471
Ow!

19:41.555 --> 19:42.931
Both sisters wield the same chop!

19:43.724 --> 19:47.686
You idiot.
If you can't even take care of yourself,

19:47.769 --> 19:50.147
no way can you take care of someone else.

19:52.191 --> 19:54.568
If you're that anxious to protect Mutsumi,

19:54.651 --> 19:57.696
then you need to understand that enduring,
without taking shortcuts,

19:57.779 --> 19:59.072
is part of your training, too.

20:00.032 --> 20:01.033
ELEMENTARY CODEBREAKING

20:01.116 --> 20:02.284
What's this?

20:03.035 --> 20:04.870
An old book of mine.

20:04.953 --> 20:07.247
Study it until you've recovered.

20:07.331 --> 20:11.001
Uh, thank you very much, Big Sis Futaba.

20:11.543 --> 20:12.669
Take care.

20:13.462 --> 20:15.214
ELEMENTARY CODEBREAKING

20:17.758 --> 20:21.386
<i>If you think that you can get by
on emotion, you're just being naive.</i>

20:23.096 --> 20:24.890
Looks like I'm the one who's naive.

20:26.099 --> 20:28.602
<i>Normally, if you drove yourself
that close to the brink,</i>

20:28.685 --> 20:31.271
<i>your soul would be destroyed
before your body.</i>

20:31.980 --> 20:37.069
<i>What's keeping that kid going isn't
anything simple like talent or hard work.</i>

20:37.569 --> 20:38.570
<i>It's emotion.</i>

20:39.404 --> 20:43.033
<i>His love for Mutsumi,
which must be close to insanity.</i>

20:43.116 --> 20:45.619
<i>All righty! How do you like that, Mutsumi?</i>

20:45.702 --> 20:47.496
<i>Big Sis, you're amazing!</i>

20:48.121 --> 20:51.833
<i>Who knows, that kid just might be</i>

20:52.501 --> 20:55.963
<i>more fit to protect Mutsumi
than I imagined.</i>

21:05.806 --> 21:06.807
I...

21:06.890 --> 21:09.268
You did it!

21:09.351 --> 21:13.105
Awesome! You finally managed
to open the bathroom door, too!

21:13.188 --> 21:15.816
That's great, Taiyo! Congratulations!

21:15.899 --> 21:17.442
Congrats!

21:18.485 --> 21:20.237
Hey, nice going!

21:20.320 --> 21:22.698
Congrats! Big Bro Taiyo!

21:22.781 --> 21:25.993
Huh.
Tossing him in the air for that?

21:26.076 --> 21:27.911
<i>Can't just be honest
for once, eh?</i>

21:28.453 --> 21:30.372
You guys, thanks a lot!

21:32.791 --> 21:34.126
It's all right.

21:34.209 --> 21:39.047
That's just the special alloy of your ring
reacting to this house's magnetic waves.

21:39.631 --> 21:44.511
It means that you've been acknowledged
as a member of the Yozakura family.

21:46.138 --> 21:48.181
Good work over the past month.

21:48.724 --> 21:52.811
From now on, we'll be training you
vigorously as a Yozakura,

21:52.894 --> 21:54.896
so keep up the good work, Taiyo!

21:55.689 --> 21:56.940
Right!

21:57.482 --> 22:02.154
Taiyo, let's have you get changed
into this 100-kilogram T-shirt right away.

22:02.237 --> 22:04.781
And I'll go ahead and change
the difficulty level of the traps

22:04.865 --> 22:06.199
from normal to very hard.

22:06.283 --> 22:07.492
What?!

22:07.576 --> 22:09.369
Taiyo, give it all you've got!

22:09.453 --> 22:11.455
Hang in there!
That's right!

22:12.080 --> 22:15.042
All right,
everybody, let's get cracking!

23:47.968 --> 23:50.887
NEXT TIME
KENGO/SHINZO
